  "street_name": "MAYESBROOK ROAD",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed first-floor rear extension, by reason of its siting, design, scale and appearance, would form an incongruous and visually intrusive addition that would fail to respect the established character, symmetry and appearance of the terrace row and would cause harm to the significance of the Becontree Estate Non-Designated Heritage Asset. The proposal is therefore contrary to:National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (August, 2026);Policies D1, D4, D5 and D6 of the London Plan (March, 2021);Policies SPP6, DMD1, DMD5 and SP2 of The Barking and Dagenham’s Local Plan (September 2024); andThe Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (February 2012)The Becontree Estate SPD &amp; Design Code (May 2026)"
